{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why."}],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Performance","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"title":"Related Documentation"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The binary-size budget","type":"heading","anchor":"The-binary-size-budget"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI builds "},{"code":"swift build -c release","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on every push and sums the resulting "},{"code":".o","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sizes for the "},{"code":"ScreenStates","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json"},{"text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxBytes"},{"type":"text","text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee","text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" each store their running "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" in a private "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentTask"},{"type":"text","text":" property, read by "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":". Every one of those "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":"s captures "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self"},{"type":"text","text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In practice, a completed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"running"}]},{"type":"text","text":" operation: without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation"},{"type":"text","text":" for the rest of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" safety net this guarantee supports."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders","text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" only ever go active once "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" have confirmed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" is already "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — both fall back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" can never be observed alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parent view that reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.state"},{"type":"text","text":" (via "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" — the pattern "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" property read in a SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":". This guarantee is about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}]},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" case could be affected."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give any screen a standard "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Empty"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Loading"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" state, usable from both UIKit and SwiftUI."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"ScreenStates"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/refresh(_:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/load(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", but keeps any data already in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" on screen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operation"},{"type":"text","text":" runs instead of switching to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":" — the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pattern behind pull-to-refresh, where the list shouldn’t disappear"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while it’s being refetched. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"duration. On success "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" is replaced as usual; on failure "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is left alone and the error is reported via "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/refresh(_:)","title":"refresh(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refresh"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" () "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A10StateStoreC5Valuexmfp","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/cancel()":{"abstract":[{"text":"Cancels whatever ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry"},{"text":" call is currently in flight, if","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"text":" (and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"text":") are left exactly as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were — cancelling never surfaces a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"text":" through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"text":", unlike letting ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operation"},{"text":" itself fail.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/cancel()","title":"cancel()","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/refreshCollection(_:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", but maps an empty result to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":", matching "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadCollect